    "caveats": [
      "Confirm the intended cell type: 0.73 Pa shear is at the upper end of microvascular endothelium (0.1–1 Pa) but ~5× above hepatic sinusoidal shear (0.05–0.15 Pa); if modeling liver sinusoids, reduce flow to ~1.5–4 µL/min.",
      "Verify the medium viscosity of 0.0035 Pa·s — it is ~3.5× water-like and directly scales both shear and pressure drop.",
      "Pressure drop ~135 Pa (~1.4 mbar) is trivial for a syringe pump but must be checked if a gravity/pumpless drive is used.",
